        {
            "id": "https://skullbuns.com/bat-party-massacre.html",
            "url": "https://skullbuns.com/bat-party-massacre.html",
            "title": "Bat Party Massacre",
            "summary": "BPM was my first 3D game and an entry to a Vaporwave themed game jam. BAT PARTY MASSACRE is a&hellip;",
            "content_html": "<p></p>\n<h2></h2>\n<h2>Overview/Goal</h2>\n<p>BPM was my first 3D game and an entry to a Vaporwave themed game jam. </p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>BAT PARTY MASSACRE</strong> is a first-person puzzle game where you play as a hyper-intelligent bat. You prey on humans during the night, sucking their blood and turning them into mindless drones. To achieve this, you are tasked with finding a path to a new target each night with clever tactics such as unlocking doors, breaking obstacles and scaring them. - Bat Party Massacre page</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h2>Media/Gallery</h2>\n<div class=\"gallery-wrapper\"><div class=\"gallery\" data-is-empty=\"false\" data-translation=\"Add images\" data-columns=\"3\">\n<figure class=\"gallery__item\"><a href=\"https://skullbuns.com/media/posts/6/gallery/sgmXah.png\" data-size=\"954x547\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://skullbuns.com/media/posts/6/gallery/sgmXah-thumbnail.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"768\" height=\"440\"></a></figure>\n<figure class=\"gallery__item\"><a href=\"https://skullbuns.com/media/posts/6/gallery/J1uXEf.png\" data-size=\"953x533\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://skullbuns.com/media/posts/6/gallery/J1uXEf-thumbnail.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"768\" height=\"430\"></a></figure>\n<figure class=\"gallery__item\"><a href=\"https://skullbuns.com/media/posts/6/gallery/WMmaKF.png\" data-size=\"956x536\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://skullbuns.com/media/posts/6/gallery/WMmaKF-thumbnail.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"768\" height=\"431\"></a></figure>\n<figure class=\"gallery__item\"><a href=\"https://skullbuns.com/media/posts/6/gallery/3zxGjP.png\" data-size=\"961x538\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://skullbuns.com/media/posts/6/gallery/3zxGjP-thumbnail.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"768\" height=\"430\"></a></figure>\n<figure class=\"gallery__item\"><a href=\"https://skullbuns.com/media/posts/6/gallery/oT1n86.png\" data-size=\"957x539\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://skullbuns.com/media/posts/6/gallery/oT1n86-thumbnail.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"768\" height=\"433\"></a></figure>\n</div></div>\n<h2>Contribution</h2>\n<p> </p>\n<h3>Tools used</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Godot Engine\n<ul>\n<li>GDScript (Programming)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Krita (2D Graphics)</li>\n<li>Blender (3D Models)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>My Role</h3>\n<p>I created the game mostly solo, from concept to production.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>I experimented with shaders using Godot's GLSL inspired shading language to create the ocean grid &amp; wave vertex movement.</li>\n<li>I began learning and using hard-surface modelling for my games through free online tutorials</li>\n<li>I ensured the game stuck to its Vaporwave art direction</li>\n<li>I programmed the bats controls, a rudimentary dialogue system and the interactions between picking things up and the world/characters.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>I did get help with playtesting and voice-acting from friends,</p>\n<h2>Reflection</h2>\n<p>I am glad I pushed myself to finally make a 3D Game. It had its own new challenges but the end result.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://itch.io/jam/vaporwave-love-game-jam/rate/2920127\">Feedback on the jam page</a> was very positive, with the most common approval being in how the theme/aethstetic was done.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>",
            "image": "https://skullbuns.com/media/posts/6/ToZxqI.png",
            "author": {
                "name": "Sophie Wheldon"
            },
            "tags": [
                   "Godot",
                   "Game Jam"
            ],
            "date_published": "2025-12-15T14:25:31+00:00",
            "date_modified": "2025-12-15T15:42:31+00:00"
