        {
            "id": "https://skullbuns.com/3d-animations-level-5-degree.html",
            "url": "https://skullbuns.com/3d-animations-level-5-degree.html",
            "title": "Level 5 3D Animations",
            "summary": "In this second year module, we were tasked with creating the following four animations: Final Showreel I really enjoyed working&hellip;",
            "content_html": "<p id=\"mcetoc_1ja9d993o56\"></p>\n<h2 id=\"mcetoc_1ja9d993o57\"></h2>\n<div class=\"post__toc\">\n<h3>Table of Contents</h3>\n<ul>\n<li> </li>\n<li><a href=\"#mcetoc_1ja9d993o58\">Overview/Goal</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#mcetoc_1ja9d993o59\">Media/Gallery</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#mcetoc_1ja9d993o5a\">Contribution</a>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"#mcetoc_1ja9d993o5b\">My Role</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#mcetoc_1ja9d993o5c\">Tools used</a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><a href=\"#mcetoc_1ja9d993o5d\">Reflection</a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"mcetoc_1ja9d993o58\">Overview/Goal</h2>\n<p>In this second year module, we were tasked with creating the following four animations:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>A lipsync to an audio of our choice using a premade-up rig (blendshapes and bones) (15 seconds / 375 frames)</li>\n<li>A bouncy ball course animation (10 seconds / 250 frames)</li>\n<li>A character interacting with an object conveying weight (10 seconds / 250 frames)</li>\n<li>2 characters dancing or fighting (10 seconds / 250 frames)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"mcetoc_1ja9d993o59\">Media/Gallery</h2>\n<h2>Final</h2>\n<p><a href=\"https://youtu.be/snlZUcDc0M4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Final Showreel</a></p>\n<h2>Progress <figure class=\"post__image\"><img loading=\"lazy\"  src=\"https://skullbuns.com/media/posts/2/Tito_Portfolio_Frames_0_To_115.mp4\" alt=\"\" width=\"NaN\" height=\"NaN\"></figure></h2>\n<h2 id=\"mcetoc_1ja9d993o5a\">Contribution</h2>\n<h3 id=\"mcetoc_1ja9d993o5b\">My Role</h3>\n<h3 id=\"mcetoc_1ja9d993o5c\">Tools used</h3>\n<p> </p>\n<h2 id=\"mcetoc_1ja9d993o5d\">Reflection</h2>\n<p>I really enjoyed working on this module! My favourite part was the lipsync - using an audio clip I already find funny and adding humourous expressions whilst Tito talks was a really enjoyable way to showcase my knowledge on how to use blendshapes and bones to give life to a 3d character.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>",
